    "created_at": "2016-11-11T08:57:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-11T08:57:48Z",
    "body": "I think “this specification” is more precise in context. But that said I can understand somebody instead reasonably seeing “this standard” as more precise. And maybe I’m biased in that I don’t much like describing what we do as ”standards”; I personally prefer to frame it more as creating new technologies for the Web, and we make specifications that document those technologies.\n\nSo I don’t see a compelling need to change “this specification”—especially if we’re already using that term consistently—but I also don’t feel strongly that the “this standard” wording is actually be bad.\n",
